{"step_index":5377,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T16:26:00Z","thinking":"Analyzing item matching within the `coordinator`. Exact text matches are prioritized. A normalized version of the shortage item's name is checked against a pre-normalized warehouse item list. If an exact match is found, it's recorded with high confidence. Otherwise, a similarity comparison needs to be performed to generate a list of candidates.\n\n\nConsidering candidates from the similarity search. The top candidate's score and brand similarity are assessed for an automatic match. If the initial criteria aren't met, an attempt to extract and compare brand tokens and dosage forms from the shortage and candidate names is performed.\nForm compatibility between the shortage and candidate items is checked, allowing for some variations such as tablets and capsules, or creams and ointments.\n\n\nNow evaluating dosage form compatibility, allowing for injections and ampoules to be considered equivalent. Checking if there are discrepancies between syrup and solid forms, specifically when a solid form in milligrams is present while the other item is a syrup. Also checking if the presence of 'co' prefix matches between the shortage and the candidate.\n\nExtracting and comparing strength patterns from the names for a precise dosage match.\n\n\nThe auto-matching rule is being applied; if dosage strength and potential prefix matches (`co_ok`) along with other criteria are satisfied, the items are automatically considered a match with high confidence. Otherwise, the top three candidates are prepared for LLM processing, along with the shortage item's name to form a specific case. These cases are collected into batches and then processed.\n\n\nAnalyzing LLM result statuses to determine the next action: a \"match\" indicates a confident identification, \"review\" requires human oversight, and \"no_match\" necessitates further evaluation. Cases deemed \"no_match\" are re-evaluated if a plausible brand connection is present among similarity search candidates, routing them to \"review\" to avoid data loss. Dosage form and prefix mismatches are used to filter out candidates.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"d:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\Pharmacy-agy\\\\src\\\\output\\\\excel_writer.py\"","EndLine":"60","StartLine":"1","toolAction":"\"Viewing excel_writer.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Inspect write_results_excel logic\""}}]}
